            </div>
            <div purpose="image-caption">
              <h5>Every change reviewed before it ships</h5>
              <p>Keep profiles, policies, and software in git. Changes go through a pull request, so you know who changed what and can roll it back.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <div purpose="feature-image">
              <img alt="Running a live query across devices" src="/images/run-query-800x537@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="image-caption">
              <h5>Linux treated like everything else</h5>
              <p>Linux laptops get the same inventory, policies, scripts, and lock and wipe as your Macs and PCs.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="page-section" id="migration">
        <div purpose="section-with-image">
          <div purpose="feature-text">
            <h3>Migration: what most teams get wrong</h3>
            <p>Most teams never try. They assume leaving Workspace ONE means wiping every device and enrolling everyone again. It doesn’t. Macs, iPhones, and iPads move through Apple’s native MDM migration with no factory reset. Windows and Linux move with Fleet’s migration scripts, so nobody re-enrolls or loses data. Run Fleet next to Workspace ONE, move one group at a time, and people keep working through it.</p>
            <div purpose="section-buttons">
              <a purpose="cta-button" class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact?talkToUs">Get a demo</a>
              <animated-arrow-button href="#compare">Fleet vs. Workspace ONE</animated-arrow-button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="section-image">
            <img alt="A device's details in Fleet after migration" src="/images/mdm-feature-image-1-344x288@2x.png">
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
